1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,780
Some purchases are too big to pay at once.

2
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:08,124
An installment plan lets a customer pay a down payment today, and the

3
00:00:08,124 --> 00:00:10,035
rest in scheduled payments.

4
00:00:10,035 --> 00:00:13,916
This video shows how to set one up, what you and the customer

5
00:00:13,916 --> 00:00:18,376
see, what happens when a card is declined, and how customers can choose

6
00:00:18,376 --> 00:00:21,040
installments for themselves at checkout.

7
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:29,134
A kitchen remodel, a course, a piece of equipment:

8
00:00:29,134 --> 00:00:32,940
many sales are easier to close when the price is split.

9
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:39,380
You want the first payment today, and the rest collected on time, without chasing anyone.

10
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:43,270
The customer wants to know what they will pay, and when.

11
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:46,470
An installment plan gives both:

12
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:52,230
a down payment, then a fixed schedule, collected from a saved card or by invoice.

13
00:00:56,430 --> 00:01:00,241
A plan has a total, a down payment, and a number of payments

14
00:01:00,241 --> 00:01:02,840
after it, which split the rest equally.

15
00:01:03,590 --> 00:01:08,506
The payments fall due every week, every two weeks, every month or every

16
00:01:08,506 --> 00:01:11,890
three months, from a first due date you choose.

17
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:16,898
They are collected by charging the card kept at the down payment, or

18
00:01:16,898 --> 00:01:18,740
by invoicing the customer.

19
00:01:19,490 --> 00:01:24,441
Every payment is also a transaction, so it shows in Transactions, and in

20
00:01:24,441 --> 00:01:26,790
the customer's My Transactions.

21
00:01:30,998 --> 00:01:33,498
Open Settings, Installment Plans.

22
00:01:33,498 --> 00:01:37,920
Collect scheduled payments by sets what a new plan starts with:

23
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:42,662
charging the saved card on each due date, or invoicing the customer.

24
00:01:42,662 --> 00:01:45,418
You can still change it on each plan.

25
00:01:45,875 --> 00:01:50,949
Retry a declined card after lists the days to wait after each failed charge:

26
00:01:50,949 --> 00:01:53,238
by default one, three and five.

27
00:01:53,238 --> 00:01:58,065
Leave it empty to hand a declined payment to the customer straight away.

28
00:01:58,519 --> 00:02:02,824
Installments at checkout lets customers split a balance themselves.

29
00:02:02,824 --> 00:02:07,601
Offer for balances from picks the kinds of balance, and Numbers of payments

30
00:02:07,601 --> 00:02:10,844
offered picks the choices, such as three and six.

31
00:02:10,844 --> 00:02:14,619
Smallest balance keeps small balances for payment in full.

32
00:02:18,825 --> 00:02:22,786
Open Subscriptions, Installment Plans, and click New plan.

33
00:02:22,786 --> 00:02:26,005
The list is empty until you make a first plan.

34
00:02:26,457 --> 00:02:29,569
Choose an existing customer, or enter a new one:

35
00:02:29,569 --> 00:02:31,125
a name, and an email.

36
00:02:31,125 --> 00:02:35,333
A new customer gets an account with that email, and sets a password

37
00:02:35,333 --> 00:02:38,387
with Forgot password when they want to sign in.

38
00:02:38,846 --> 00:02:42,140
Say what the plan is for, such as Kitchen remodel.

39
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:47,021
Enter the total, the down payment today, and the number of payments after it.

40
00:02:47,021 --> 00:02:50,609
Choose how often they fall due, and the first due date.

41
00:02:50,609 --> 00:02:51,256
Here:

42
00:02:51,256 --> 00:02:55,666
twelve hundred dollars, three hundred down, and six monthly payments.

43
00:02:56,134 --> 00:03:00,381
The Schedule card shows every payment, its date and its amount:

44
00:03:00,381 --> 00:03:03,336
six payments of one hundred fifty dollars.

45
00:03:03,336 --> 00:03:05,859
Then choose how they are collected:

46
00:03:05,859 --> 00:03:10,844
charge the card on each due date, or invoice the customer for each payment.

47
00:03:11,372 --> 00:03:13,697
Click Continue to the down payment.

48
00:03:13,697 --> 00:03:17,554
The plan is saved as Waiting for down payment, and the page to

49
00:03:17,554 --> 00:03:19,482
take the down payment opens.

50
00:03:23,643 --> 00:03:27,938
The list shows each plan with its status, the customer, the total, what

51
00:03:27,938 --> 00:03:31,564
was received and what is outstanding, and the next payment.

52
00:03:31,564 --> 00:03:33,293
Open a plan to manage it.

53
00:03:33,757 --> 00:03:35,752
The plan page has a Summary:

54
00:03:35,752 --> 00:03:40,738
its status, the customer, the total, what was received and what is outstanding,

55
00:03:40,738 --> 00:03:44,082
how the payments are collected, and who created it.

56
00:03:44,082 --> 00:03:49,713
Payments lists the down payment and every scheduled payment, with its status and due date.

57
00:03:49,713 --> 00:03:53,057
History lists everything that happened to the plan.

58
00:03:53,527 --> 00:03:56,836
While a plan is not finished, you can cancel it.

59
00:03:56,836 --> 00:04:01,064
Enter a reason if you like, click Cancel the plan, and confirm.

60
00:04:01,064 --> 00:04:05,170
Payments already received stay received, and can be refunded.

61
00:04:05,170 --> 00:04:07,927
Payments not yet received are canceled.

62
00:04:12,127 --> 00:04:17,344
Taking the down payment needs a payment provider that can keep a card, such as Stripe.

63
00:04:17,344 --> 00:04:22,617
This demonstration site has none connected, so the next steps are described, not shown.

64
00:04:23,367 --> 00:04:27,925
On the Take the down payment page, you enter the card, and click Charge.

65
00:04:27,925 --> 00:04:32,657
When the payment is confirmed, the plan is Active, and the schedule starts.

66
00:04:33,407 --> 00:04:38,634
On each due date, the saved card is charged, or the customer is invoiced.

67
00:04:38,634 --> 00:04:44,787
A few days before, the customer is reminded, and after each payment they get a receipt.

68
00:04:45,537 --> 00:04:50,383
Charge now collects a payment before its due date, or tries a declined

69
00:04:50,383 --> 00:04:55,357
card again at once, on an Active or Past due plan that charges the card.

70
00:04:59,557 --> 00:05:04,083
If a card is declined, the payment is marked Failed, the plan becomes

71
00:05:04,083 --> 00:05:08,247
Past due, and the customer is told when it will be tried again.

72
00:05:08,997 --> 00:05:12,271
The card is tried again after the days you set:

73
00:05:12,271 --> 00:05:14,556
by default one, three and five.

74
00:05:14,556 --> 00:05:17,645
After the last try, the payment becomes Due:

75
00:05:17,645 --> 00:05:23,327
a balance the customer pays from My Transactions, and the overdue reminders take over.

76
00:05:24,077 --> 00:05:30,524
A plan is Waiting for down payment, Active, Past due, Completed or Canceled.

77
00:05:30,524 --> 00:05:35,477
Each payment is Scheduled, Due, Paid, Failed or Canceled.

78
00:05:39,677 --> 00:05:43,346
Customers can also choose installments themselves.

79
00:05:43,346 --> 00:05:48,652
When they pay an outstanding balance, checkout can offer Choose how to pay:

80
00:05:48,652 --> 00:05:52,517
Pay in full, or, for example, three monthly payments.

81
00:05:53,267 --> 00:05:56,982
Choosing installments makes a plan with no down payment:

82
00:05:56,982 --> 00:06:01,716
the first payment is charged in the same checkout, and the card is saved.

83
00:06:01,716 --> 00:06:06,450
Once it is received, the plan replaces the original balance, and the rest

84
00:06:06,450 --> 00:06:08,487
is charged on its due dates.

85
00:06:09,237 --> 00:06:13,609
If the customer leaves checkout without paying, the plan is closed, and they

86
00:06:13,609 --> 00:06:15,582
still owe the original balance.

87
00:06:15,582 --> 00:06:18,887
You turn this on in the plan settings, as shown earlier.

88
00:06:23,087 --> 00:06:24,318
A contractor:

89
00:06:24,318 --> 00:06:28,077
a down payment, then monthly payments for a remodel.

90
00:06:28,827 --> 00:06:30,503
A training provider:

91
00:06:30,503 --> 00:06:32,887
a course fee in three payments.

92
00:06:33,637 --> 00:06:35,390
An equipment seller:

93
00:06:35,390 --> 00:06:38,627
a card kept, and charged on each due date.

94
00:06:39,377 --> 00:06:40,359
A store:

95
00:06:40,359 --> 00:06:43,867
customers split a large balance at checkout.

96
00:06:45,867 --> 00:06:51,358
With installment plans, a bigger sale is easier to say yes to, and easier to collect.

97
00:06:51,358 --> 00:06:52,927
Thanks for watching.

